# Essence spam: guarantee maximum Life on a pair of boots while fishing the
# random (non-guaranteed) mods for a top-tier elemental resistance.
#
# NOTE: this is a DESIGN TARGET — it uses features still in progress:
#   * the `essence` operation,
#   * the `essence "<type>" t1` shorthand (t1 = Deafening, the best tier),
#   * `or` in predicates.
# It is not checkable yet; it shows the intended shape of an essence craft.

craft in poe1

item {
    base:   "Two-Toned Boots"
    ilvl:   84            # high enough for T1 elemental resistances to roll
    rarity: normal
}

# Deafening Essence of Greed guarantees "+ to maximum Life" and reforges every
# other mod on each application. Because it is a top tier (>= Screaming), it can
# reforge a RARE item — so after the first Normal -> Rare application the loop can
# keep re-rolling. A low-tier essence would fail here: it only upgrades Normal
# items, so the second iteration (now Rare) would have nothing to work on.
#
# `t1` selects the best tier (Deafening), the same T1-is-best convention used for
# mod tiers. We spin until the random fill happens to include a T1 fire, cold, or
# lightning resistance — any of the three is a win.
until has "fire resistance" t1
   or has "cold resistance" t1
   or has "lightning resistance" t1 {
    essence "greed" t1
}
